main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ B path: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ C path: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.virtual]/2: each of D's two A subobjects has its own final
overrider of A::f -- B::f in the one of B, A::f in the one of C -- so each
needs its own virtual table (Itanium C++ ABI 2.5: a secondary virtual table
per base subobject).  The front end rejected the class.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
